## Change log

- `[admin+app] 2026-08-13` — **Driver operations tracking.** Append-only `driver_operation_events` (staff SELECT only, in `supabase_realtime`) records every driver-app RPC: auth, device, duty, shift, location/geofence, delivery, requests, e-sign, visits, notifications, profile, security. Two emitters: `log_driver_operation` in-transaction for RPCs that return an error object, and `log_driver_operation_autonomous` over `dblink` for RPCs that `RAISE EXCEPTION` (so `active_pickup_exists`, `delivery_out_of_range`, `duplicate_order_id`, `shift_required` survive the rollback). The autonomous path reads its DSN from vault secret `driver_ops_audit_dsn` and no-ops when it is absent — `driver_ops_audit_health()` reports that, and the retention cron surfaces it to Sentry. Hot paths are deliberately partial: accepted heartbeats, no-op notification marks and unchanged app versions are not logged. `driver_locations.last_report_at` / `coalesced_since_count` give liveness without flooding realtime (throttled to 60s), and `driver_report_location` finally writes `geofence_events` on zone flips. Admin: `driver_ops.view` / `driver_ops.export`, Live Tracking **Activity** tab (keyset pagination, live pause with an "N new" pill), driver-popup timeline and a per-driver Activity tab with CSV export on `/drivers/[id]`. Migrations `20260908100000`–`20260908200000`; cron `/api/cron/driver-ops-retention` (01:20 daily).

- `[admin+app] 2026-08-13` — **The failure audit actually writes, and covers the rest of the validation failures.** The entry above shipped `log_driver_operation_autonomous` behind a Vault secret an operator was meant to create by hand from the project database password. Nobody did, so `driver_ops_audit_health()` read `secret_missing` and every Class B failure still rolled its own audit row back. `driver_ops_auditor` is now a dedicated login role whose password is generated by `gen_random_bytes` and consumed inside one `DO` block — never printed, never in git, independent of project password rotation — holding no table grants and one `EXECUTE`, on `driver_ops_audit.log_driver_operation_remote` (SECURITY DEFINER, owner `postgres`, empty `search_path`, its own schema so the role needs no `USAGE` on `public`). The DSN targets `db.<ref>.supabase.co` **because** it is remote: every loopback form matches a `trust` line in `pg_hba`, the server never asks for a password, and dblink then refuses the connection for a non-superuser. Second half: `driver_ops_fail` logs-then-reraises, closing `shift.submit` (9 validation codes), `delivery.pickup_create` / `.complete` / `.cancel` (`location_required`, `delivery_id_required`, `cancel_reason_required`, `invalid_order_id`), `auth.login_selfie` (`object_key_required`, `invalid_object_key`), plus success logging for `register_or_sync_rider_profile`. Messages and SQLSTATEs are byte-identical, verified per code. Still deliberately unlogged and now written down in [`docs/DRIVER_OPS_COVERAGE.md`](../../docs/DRIVER_OPS_COVERAGE.md): hot paths, read-only getters, callers with no driver row, and the shared `_driver_assert_*` preconditions (`device_revoked` is the top follow-up). Migrations `20260909100100`, `20260909100200`.

